1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,730
There are trends in food, much as there are trends in clothing.

2
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:12,284
Interest in food fashions has risen rapidly since the birth of the smartphone when

3
00:00:12,284 --> 00:00:18,697
people first began taking photos of their food and instantly sharing them with their

4
00:00:18,697 --> 00:00:20,040
friends.

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:25,862
The food industry in the UK, in particular, is obsessed with finding

6
00:00:25,862 --> 00:00:30,480
and exploiting the next big food trend.

7
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:35,300
Marketeers aim to create a huge demand for a food item,

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,549
which was previously unknown,

9
00:00:37,549 --> 00:00:40,240
or not needed.

10
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:45,476
One of the most effective ways of promoting a new food product is by

11
00:00:45,476 --> 00:00:50,230
using social media influencers as brand ambassadors.

12
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:57,429
In return for free samples, many influencers will post content about a product, although

13
00:00:57,429 --> 00:01:03,765
there are influencers with hundreds of thousands of followers who can command large fees

14
00:01:03,765 --> 00:01:05,650
for their services.

15
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:12,458
Companies which sell vegan produce were pioneers in being able to increase sales really

16
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:15,510
quickly in this way.

17
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:20,788
For a food item to become really popular it has to be readily available,

18
00:01:20,788 --> 00:01:27,110
so supermarkets have a role to play in creating a new food trend.

19
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:35,166
They have dedicated teams closely following which new products or ingredients are trending on social media

20
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:42,180
and are particularly interested in what well-known chefs are putting on their menus.

21
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:48,319
I’d like to look at a few examples of marketing campaigns which were really

22
00:01:48,319 --> 00:01:51,770
successful in launching a new fashion trend.

23
00:01:51,770 --> 00:01:56,320
Starting in the 1990s with the avocado.

24
00:01:56,320 --> 00:02:02,900
A British PR company was hired to raise its profile and stimulate demand.

25
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:09,022
They paid for a group of journalists to travel out to South Africa to

26
00:02:09,022 --> 00:02:11,430
meet avocado farmers.

27
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:18,845
Articles written following this visit helped to educate the British public about the avocado,

28
00:02:18,845 --> 00:02:25,980
which at this time was certainly not the daily staple it’s since become.

29
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:31,259
Advertisements were designed to promote the avocado as a ‘superfood’:

30
00:02:31,259 --> 00:02:36,840
rich in nutrients and therefore beneficial for health.

31
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:45,091
Avocados became hugely fashionable and within a few years UK avocado sales had grown

32
00:02:45,091 --> 00:02:53,322
from 13 million pounds annually to around 150 million, making it one of the

33
00:02:53,322 --> 00:02:59,350
most successful fresh produce campaigns in UK history.

34
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:05,555
Oat milk is a recent example of a new product which became fashionable very

35
00:03:05,555 --> 00:03:06,860
quickly.

36
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,568
Now there are many brands available,

37
00:03:09,568 --> 00:03:16,670
but one company which had early success was the Swedish brand, Oatly.

38
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:23,056
They attracted a lot of attention with a media campaign which used provocation as

39
00:03:23,056 --> 00:03:26,590
a way of getting their message across effectively.

40
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:34,352
The fact that this campaign aggravated competitors producing milk from dairy cows was seen

41
00:03:34,352 --> 00:03:40,410
as a plus, as it helped to make oat milk seem cool.

42
00:03:40,410 --> 00:03:47,049
In the USA, the brand decided against a big retail launch in favour of

43
00:03:47,049 --> 00:03:49,596
getting the product into coffee chains,

44
00:03:49,596 --> 00:03:54,350
which removed the need for a big advertising budget.

45
00:03:54,350 --> 00:04:00,560
This proved far more effective than offering samples in supermarkets.

46
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:07,800
Oat milk had an advantage over other alternative milk products such as almond milk.

47
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:14,080
Many consumers prefer it because it has less of an impact on the environment.

48
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:20,114
It requires significantly less water to produce than other alternative milk products

49
00:04:20,114 --> 00:04:26,770
and it also has a relatively low carbon footprint.

50
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:35,334
Norwegian skrei, a rarely available seasonal fish delicacy, otherwise known as Arctic cod, is

51
00:04:35,334 --> 00:04:40,990
now found on the menus of Michelin starred restaurants throughout Europe.

52
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:46,627
The demand for skrei has been used by a food marketing agency to build

53
00:04:46,627 --> 00:04:51,060
the reputation of Norway’s fisheries in general.

54
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:58,009
Marketing surveys have shown that a significant number of shoppers now associate Norway with

55
00:04:58,009 --> 00:05:00,660
excellent seafood.

56
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:07,285
Food trends can be considered a good thing in some ways as they can benefit farmers

57
00:05:07,285 --> 00:05:11,240
and food producers enormously.

58
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:18,010
The public can also be encouraged to buy things which are more sustainably produced.

59
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:23,788
But ethical concerns have been raised about the effects a surge in demand can

60
00:05:23,788 --> 00:05:27,880
cause.Quinoa is a classic example.

61
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,346
This plant is native to Peru,

62
00:05:30,346 --> 00:05:37,685
and when demand peaked some years ago, the price soared, making it unaffordable for

63
00:05:37,685 --> 00:05:39,570
local people.

64
00:05:39,570 --> 00:05:46,374
While the popularity of quinoa has benefitted farmers financially, there have been other negative

65
00:05:46,374 --> 00:05:48,060
consequences.

66
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:53,948
As demand grew, farmers began working the land all year round in order to

67
00:05:53,948 --> 00:05:56,500
produce more quinoa.

68
00:05:56,500 --> 00:06:02,099
One issue has been that the fertility of the soil decreased dramatically,

69
00:06:02,099 --> 00:06:08,460
which could potentially lead to desertification in some areas.

